  "provenance": [
    "DS12288 Rev6 STM32G474xx: exact RE512KiB/LQFP64; SRAM1 80KiB+SRAM2 16KiB are DMA-visible96KiB at0x20000000. CCM32KiB is declared once at0x10000000. RM0440p89 also permits DMA through its0x20018000 SRAM-bus alias; the selected linker/DMA policy deliberately excludes both CCM addresses rather than claiming a silicon restriction. Default linker and generated DMA domains select96KiB SRAM1/2 only.",
    "RM0440 Rev9: DBANK=1 required,256 physical2KiB pages; startup validates option/density/category without writing Flash. HSE24 PLLM6/N85/R2, boost170MHz/APB170MHz; TIM2 PSC169 reserved.",
    "https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/stm32g474rc.pdf",
    "https://www.st.com/resource/en/reference_manual/rm0440-stm32g4-series-advanced-armbased-32bit-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf",
    "https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/cmsis-device-g4/tree/626ee412334a5ed2e5b320af5a8d77d69f03a558",
    "DS12288 Rev6 November2021; Table12 Section4.10 LQFP64 column; Figure7 p50; Table2 p16 independently confirm52 package GPIOs. PDF SHA256 b018e20dbe34b63a43e49365518b186ef0e0e8e899deeabc1c9f53a3a10c1add. PG10 shares NRST and option-byte/electrical restrictions; inventory does not open new Board routes or provider modes.",
    "Fixed HSE24 profile reserves PF0/PF1 oscillator pads. Conditional PG10/NRST GPIO remains reserved until a reviewed option-byte/Board policy is implemented; inventory52 does not authorize these pads."
  ],
